  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Nursing, Vocational A.S. Degree - Cal-GETC GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 8, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7779/PublishedPdf), GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Official Total Units: 83-86; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 14+14+6+15+12+12+12 = 85 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page; BIOL 430 + BIOL 431 path). Semester sums verified against the map's 14-15 / 12-14 / 6 / 15 / 12 / 12 / 12 headers. PROGRAM STRUCTURE: Semesters 1-3 plus the Summer Term are prerequisites/GE (complete before program enrollment); Semesters 4-6 are the lockstep Vocational Nursing professional phase (VN 120/130/140, 12 units each, requiring admission to the LVN program). Biology path: the map offers BIOL 302 OR BIOL 430 (Semester 2); BIOL 431 (Semester 3) is ONLY required for students who took BIOL 430 — BIOL 302 takers instead complete any Cal-GETC Area 5B Biological Science course (see counselor). This seed models the BIOL 430/431 path (5+5 units) which matches the official 83-86 total and the Semester 3 '15 Units' header. Program-eligibility notes from the map: 12th-grade education or equivalent (per California Dept. of Education); BIOL 100 or BIOL 430/431 with a grade of B or better; cumulative 2.5 GPA with C or better in AH 311, EDUC 300 or PSYC 370, NUTRI 300 or 480, and PSYC C1000 or 480. Financial-aid note: students must claim Pre-Health Occupations as their major until accepted into the Nursing, Vocational program; complete GE before enrolling in the program (recommended). Choice slots: (1) ENGL C1000 (3) / ENGL 488 (4) / ESLW 340 (4); (2) EDUC 300 / PSYC 370 (Human Development: A Life Span); (3) ETHNS 300 / 320 / 330 / 350 / 360; (4) BIOL 302 / BIOL 430; (5) NUTRI 300 / NUTRI 480 Honors; (6) STAT C1000 / STAT C1000H. Cal-GETC Area 4 requires 2 courses from different disciplines (EDUC 300/PSYC 370 in Semester 1 and PSYC C1000 in the Summer Term). Prereqs per map: CHEM 305 requires Elementary Algebra; BIOL 430 requires CHEM 305/309/400; BIOL 431 requires BIOL 430; VN 120 requires admission to the LVN program; VN 130 requires VN 120; VN 140 requires VN 130. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
